 					"text": "tele runs scripts: typescript or javascript files in a scripts folder that can call any telegram method, watch every update and change requests on their way. each script is off until you turn it on, and tele asks you, in plain words, before it gets any grant. everything a script can do is in the scripting reference. tele writes typings for every telegram method and type next to your scripts, so editors complete and check them, and a script only gets the grants it declares. scripts can keep their own data on this device and look up the chats and users tele already knows. the mtproto console gets a scripts tab with your scripts and their logs, and an editor that runs code against your account right away. results in the console's script editor unfold like in a browser's devtools, and the editor and its output sit side by side. scripts declare grants like inugram plugins and can hold a request or an update while they decide what to do with it. no script can log in or out, touch your sessions or password, or read login codes. scripts get simple ways to read chats and history, send, edit, delete, forward and react to messages, and to hear about new, edited and deleted ones. scripts can download and upload files, check or rewrite your messages before they go out, and ask you things in tele's own boxes. scripts can add items to the message, chat and profile menus and get a settings page of their own. scripts can add /commands, which show up among the suggestions when you type a slash. scripts can show messages that exist only on this device and never reach telegram. scripts can change how users and chats look on this device: name, color, emoji status, premium star and verification marks. scripts have no limit on menu items, commands, boxes and toasts, and can watch every request with one grant. scripts can put badges and highlights on messages, read messages tele has already loaded, and see the messages you send yourself. scripts can open chats and profiles, 